WEBVTT

1
00:03:59.175 --> 00:04:01.409
Turn it off.

2
00:04:07.552 --> 00:04:08.867
Give me the keys.

3
00:04:22.965 --> 00:04:26.635
- How bad is it?
- I can make it.

4
00:04:27.035 --> 00:04:29.804
I only got one more day. I can make it.

5
00:04:45.671 --> 00:04:47.372
Please.

6
00:04:48.307 --> 00:04:50.023
Let me see it.

7
00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:52.551
I went straight through, thank God.

8
00:04:55.233 --> 00:04:57.469
- You got lucky.
- This is lucky?

9
00:04:58.049 --> 00:05:00.568
Yeah, darling, this is lucky.

10
00:05:01.369 --> 00:05:03.190
It's okay, baby.

11
00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:07.193
You may want to bite something.

12
00:05:15.533 --> 00:05:19.735
- Do you know what you're doing?
- Spent three years in the desert, darling.

13
00:05:24.977 --> 00:05:28.547
I need you to hold still. All right?

14
00:05:55.273 --> 00:05:57.529
Your plates are swapped.
You're good until Alabama.

15
00:05:57.909 --> 00:06:01.940
If you get woozy, you take a bump.
Not a line, a bump.

16
00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:04.216
Go straight down this road
and keep your lights off.

17
00:06:04.316 --> 00:06:07.151
You keep 'em fucking off
until you hit the pavement.

18
00:06:08.051 --> 00:06:11.187
- You understand me?
- Thank you so much.

19
00:07:00.305 --> 00:07:02.049
What's he doing?

20
00:07:03.041 --> 00:07:05.276
He's shooting rabbits.

21
00:07:05.976 --> 00:07:07.745
What's he doing that for?

22
00:07:07.845 --> 00:07:11.114
'Cause they're like squirrels,
chewing and digging everything up.

23
00:07:12.917 --> 00:07:15.653
Or maybe this is
what people do around here.

24
00:07:18.089 --> 00:07:20.690
What, is he like a tweaker or something?

25
00:07:22.159 --> 00:07:24.661
No, he's not a tweaker.

26
00:07:26.197 --> 00:07:28.372
How do you know?

27
00:07:30.568 --> 00:07:32.570
His aim's too good.

28
00:07:51.006 --> 00:07:52.773
Seriously?

29
00:07:56.528 --> 00:07:58.217
You're such a jerk.

30
00:07:59.047 --> 00:08:00.589
I'm late, babe.

31
00:08:04.836 --> 00:08:08.038
Johnny, when are you coming back?

32
00:08:09.341 --> 00:08:13.355
I don't know.
It... it shouldn't take too long.

33
00:08:24.822 --> 00:08:27.224
A few hours.
I can stop and get lunch if you want.

34
00:08:27.324 --> 00:08:29.027
No.

35
00:08:30.627 --> 00:08:32.929
What is it, then?

36
00:08:33.731 --> 00:08:35.533
Nothing.

37
00:08:50.132 --> 00:08:52.437
This is temporary.

38
00:08:53.418 --> 00:08:55.620
How temporary?

39
00:08:57.823 --> 00:09:00.764
A few more deliveries and we're cool.

40
00:09:01.426 --> 00:09:05.464
I get straight with my uncle,
and then we can get Oceanside, you know?

41
00:09:06.164 --> 00:09:08.917
Someplace nobody can find us.

42
00:09:16.023 --> 00:09:20.495
We're close, babe.
We're really, really close.

43
00:10:41.726 --> 00:10:43.929
You come in late...

44
00:10:44.329 --> 00:10:46.297
you come in short...

45
00:10:46.397 --> 00:10:49.900
and you've brought me a side of attitude.

46
00:10:53.639 --> 00:10:56.541
I've been sticking
my fucking neck out for you.

47
00:10:56.641 --> 00:10:58.175
I get it.

48
00:10:58.275 --> 00:11:00.445
You know, I read that...

49
00:11:01.045 --> 00:11:05.448
the number one reason
people give for office theft...

50
00:11:06.384 --> 00:11:09.387
is "the company owes me something."

51
00:11:13.191 --> 00:11:17.298
You see that employee right there?
My nephew.

52
00:11:20.131 --> 00:11:22.133
He knows how to do his job.

53
00:11:22.433 --> 00:11:24.756
He keeps it clean.

54
00:11:25.036 --> 00:11:29.041
And he knows that
I don't owe nobody jack shit.

55
00:11:29.341 --> 00:11:32.044
That's why he's gonna grow old and fat.

56
00:11:32.644 --> 00:11:36.147
And you... I don't know about you.

57
00:11:37.716 --> 00:11:41.652
Guille, get this jackass out of here
before I lose my temper.

58
00:11:44.955 --> 00:11:47.192
Sorry to keep ya.

59
00:11:48.193 --> 00:11:50.528
Training day.

60
00:11:51.428 --> 00:11:56.000
- Big delivery today, John.
- Oh, yeah? What should I expect?

61
00:11:56.100 --> 00:11:59.671
100. Not a penny less.

62
00:12:00.171 --> 00:12:02.840
- 100.
- Light me a goddamn cigarette.

63
00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:05.377
Go on, Guille.

64
00:12:05.977 --> 00:12:07.766
How's things out at the ranch?

65
00:12:07.866 --> 00:12:10.999
Rosie's complaining about the bugs a little,
but other than that, everything's good.

66
00:12:11.099 --> 00:12:13.435
You're doing pretty good for yourself?

67
00:12:14.185 --> 00:12:16.253
No problems, right?

68
00:12:16.353 --> 00:12:21.159
So if anything was bothering you,
you'd tell me, right?

69
00:12:22.261 --> 00:12:24.539
I mean, yeah, of course.

70
00:12:24.639 --> 00:12:27.240
Of course I would. Everything's good.

71
00:12:30.736 --> 00:12:32.270
You...

72
00:12:33.070 --> 00:12:35.541
your daddy was like you.

73
00:12:35.641 --> 00:12:37.943
The devil keep his soul.

74
00:12:38.043 --> 00:12:40.401
He didn't say much...

75
00:12:40.501 --> 00:12:42.480
but when he did...

76
00:12:46.550 --> 00:12:52.189
He saved my neck more times
than I can even think about.

77
00:12:52.289 --> 00:12:55.526
I owed him, you see?

78
00:12:55.626 --> 00:12:59.631
And that's why I took you in,
taught you how to be a man, you know?

79
00:12:59.731 --> 00:13:03.268
I mean, you said you wanted
to go in the Service.

80
00:13:03.368 --> 00:13:05.370
I allowed it.

81
00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:09.441
- Yeah.
- But that's over now, John, you know?

82
00:13:09.541 --> 00:13:15.213
You've done your time.
You at home now with family, right?

83
00:13:15.313 --> 00:13:18.283
Where you belong, no?

84
00:13:18.383 --> 00:13:20.118
I know, Neil.

85
00:13:21.519 --> 00:13:25.154
- Uncle Neil.
- Uncle Neil.

86
00:13:25.756 --> 00:13:27.524
Yeah.

87
00:13:28.626 --> 00:13:29.660
Yeah.

88
00:15:22.973 --> 00:15:24.718
Is there a problem, Officer?

89
00:15:24.818 --> 00:15:27.511
Step out of the vehicle.

90
00:15:36.019 --> 00:15:38.590
Have an appointment today, Johnny?

91
00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:41.726
Make a little pickup from your uncle?

92
00:15:41.826 --> 00:15:45.949
- I'm clean.
- Bullshit. You was born dirty.

93
00:15:47.898 --> 00:15:50.768
You know better
than to leave it out in the open.

94
00:15:50.868 --> 00:15:53.571
Maybe you're hiding it someplace else.

95
00:15:53.671 --> 00:15:57.123
Someplace I gotta look
a little harder to find.

96
00:15:58.343 --> 00:16:01.779
You think I don't know
what goes on here, Johnny?

97
00:16:02.179 --> 00:16:05.816
Your kind rots this town
from the inside out.

98
00:16:05.916 --> 00:16:10.154
And I don't take no shit
from two-bit dirt rats like you.

99
00:16:10.254 --> 00:16:15.586
No matter what your tats say,
you'll always be scum under my boots.

100
00:16:19.130 --> 00:16:22.832
- What you say to me?
- I just said you're not wrong.

101
00:16:27.270 --> 00:16:30.975
You're clean. Guess you weren't lying.

102
00:16:31.175 --> 00:16:33.476
Drive safe, Johnny.

103
00:18:12.743 --> 00:18:15.245
What happened to you?

104
00:18:16.346 --> 00:18:18.614
It ain't mine.

105
00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:25.989
How's that gal of yours?

106
00:18:26.089 --> 00:18:28.091
She's sick.

107
00:18:29.327 --> 00:18:31.563
Is she inside?

108
00:18:32.063 --> 00:18:33.864
Nope.

109
00:18:36.234 --> 00:18:38.236
Well, I hope she's all right.

110
00:18:48.912 --> 00:18:51.314
See ya in a few days.

111
00:19:10.267 --> 00:19:12.460
Hey, what happened?

112
00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:14.637
All good.

113
00:19:24.215 --> 00:19:26.724
There was a good amount.

114
00:19:26.824 --> 00:19:28.947
How much?

115
00:19:29.886 --> 00:19:32.855
I think it was like 100 grand
or something.

116
00:19:34.341 --> 00:19:36.779
100 grand?

117
00:19:38.061 --> 00:19:40.464
How much of that do we get?

118
00:19:41.366 --> 00:19:43.000
25.

119
00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:47.905
Tomorrow, the white bag goes to Neil,
and we get the fuck out of here.

120
00:19:48.805 --> 00:19:51.409
I knew you could do it.
I knew you could do it.

121
00:19:54.544 --> 00:19:56.979
I knew we could do it.

122
00:20:33.584 --> 00:20:36.120
What if we took all of it?

123
00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:39.722
Neil would hunt us down and kill us.

124
00:20:48.366 --> 00:20:50.888
Is he gonna kill us if we leave?

125
00:20:50.988 --> 00:20:55.438
Well, not fucking him over
would certainly help him cope.

126
00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:02.413
We could really use the whole 100.

127
00:21:02.513 --> 00:21:06.518
Yeah, we could, right?
It'd certainly make a difference.

128
00:21:06.618 --> 00:21:10.337
That would be greedy.
Greed makes people unlucky.

129
00:21:15.223 --> 00:21:17.061
Yeah?

130
00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:20.298
Hey, neighbor.

131
00:21:20.398 --> 00:21:24.301
Hey, listen, I hate to bother you so late,
but, got a question for you.

132
00:21:24.401 --> 00:21:26.104
All right.

133
00:21:26.204 --> 00:21:28.840
Brought over a couple cold ones.

134
00:21:29.940 --> 00:21:31.576
Yeah, come on in.

135
00:21:31.676 --> 00:21:34.979
- All right, cool, thanks.
- Have a seat over there.

136
00:21:35.879 --> 00:21:37.948
Thank you.

137
00:21:46.756 --> 00:21:49.706
- What's he want?
- I don't know.

138
00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:57.901
- So what's going on?
- I appreciate it.

139
00:21:58.001 --> 00:21:59.736
Yeah.

140
00:22:02.440 --> 00:22:04.749
By any chance, were you on my land today?

141
00:22:04.849 --> 00:22:08.779
Yeah. Yeah, your trashcan was laying
in the middle of the road.

142
00:22:08.879 --> 00:22:11.069
Just drug it back up to your house.

143
00:22:11.169 --> 00:22:13.050
All right.

144
00:22:13.150 --> 00:22:15.352
Makes me feel better.

145
00:22:15.452 --> 00:22:18.755
Found some tracks, you know, I didn't know
if someone was trying to rob me or whatever.

146
00:22:18.855 --> 00:22:21.459
Hell, you can't tell about people
in these parts.

147
00:22:21.559 --> 00:22:24.027
Nope, that was just me.

148
00:22:26.430 --> 00:22:29.366
You gonna keep peeking around
that corner or you gonna come out?

149
00:22:36.406 --> 00:22:39.109
- Good to meet you.
- How you doing?

150
00:22:39.209 --> 00:22:40.977
I'm Rosie.

151
00:22:44.714 --> 00:22:48.104
We don't get too many women
good-looking as you around these parts.

152
00:22:54.891 --> 00:22:57.092
Y'all married?

153
00:22:59.629 --> 00:23:01.397
Yeah.

154
00:23:03.100 --> 00:23:05.201
All right.

155
00:23:08.471 --> 00:23:11.039
Just wondering who you was.

156
00:23:13.109 --> 00:23:15.147
I'm Rosie.

157
00:23:16.347 --> 00:23:18.549
Night, baby.

158
00:23:22.152 --> 00:23:24.754
Yeah, I got me one of those.

159
00:23:27.158 --> 00:23:29.194
Yeah, they're pretty good
for looking at the stars.

160
00:23:29.294 --> 00:23:32.095
I use mine for looking at my neighbors.

161
00:23:37.233 --> 00:23:39.937
I'm just screwing with you,
John boy, come on.

162
00:23:42.340 --> 00:23:47.311
No, but I do watch that road out front.
See some pretty interesting things.

163
00:23:49.913 --> 00:23:53.950
Sometimes a car will come in light
with one pair of plates.

164
00:23:55.585 --> 00:23:59.850
Hour later, goes out heavy
with another pair of plates.

165
00:24:01.057 --> 00:24:03.359
Ain't that weird?

166
00:24:04.828 --> 00:24:07.264
We all got our secrets.

167
00:24:07.364 --> 00:24:09.733
I ain't no hypocrite.

168
00:24:09.833 --> 00:24:13.136
You do what you do, I do what I do.

169
00:24:14.671 --> 00:24:18.342
That's why we live out in these parts.
Don't want to be bothered by others.

170
00:24:20.176 --> 00:24:24.316
Well, I better be heading on back.
My boys gonna be gettin' home at any second.

171
00:24:25.016 --> 00:24:29.487
Hey, come on by sometime.
I owe you for a cold one.

172
00:24:30.087 --> 00:24:32.388
Nighty night, neighbor.

173
00:26:54.398 --> 00:26:56.427
Stop being nosy, babe.

174
00:26:56.527 --> 00:27:00.236
And pack your bags, we gotta go
as soon as I get back, all right?

175
00:27:11.247 --> 00:27:13.950
Are you sure you're ready for this?

176
00:27:14.350 --> 00:27:16.151
Yeah.

177
00:27:17.604 --> 00:27:21.725
Yeah? Leaving everyone?
Friends and family and everyone?

178
00:27:21.825 --> 00:27:24.326
We don't have any friends.

179
00:27:33.903 --> 00:27:35.639
This...

180
00:27:56.727 --> 00:27:58.963
I'll see ya, babe.

181
00:28:32.562 --> 00:28:34.884
Should just buy everything new.

182
00:29:52.309 --> 00:29:56.945
- Hey, any bumps on the road?
- Nope. All good.

183
00:29:57.682 --> 00:29:59.683
All right.

184
00:30:02.402 --> 00:30:04.305
Here you go.

185
00:30:04.405 --> 00:30:06.289
Try this.

186
00:30:06.389 --> 00:30:08.426
I'm not that hungry, but...

187
00:30:08.826 --> 00:30:11.627
I didn't ask you if you were hungry.

188
00:30:13.363 --> 00:30:14.522
Where you going, John?

189
00:30:14.622 --> 00:30:16.869
I'm not going anywhere.
What the fuck are you talking about?

190
00:30:16.969 --> 00:30:20.046
This is a small town, boy.
There's no secrets I don't hear.

191
00:30:20.146 --> 00:30:22.245
I don't know what you're listening to,
but it's bullshit.

192
00:30:22.345 --> 00:30:24.308
- Bullshit?
- Why would I fuck you over?

193
00:30:24.408 --> 00:30:27.109
You're the only family I got.

194
00:30:29.313 --> 00:30:31.715
You are right for Hallmark, boy.

195
00:30:35.218 --> 00:30:38.488
I hear everything. Everything.

196
00:30:38.588 --> 00:30:41.725
Sometimes I hear things I don't like.

197
00:30:41.825 --> 00:30:46.630
Now, I rely on a lot of people.
Most especially you.

198
00:30:47.430 --> 00:30:49.977
I can't afford for there
to be any dissension.

199
00:30:51.535 --> 00:30:53.369
You understand?

200
00:30:53.969 --> 00:30:56.432
Even if we are family...

201
00:31:15.691 --> 00:31:19.329
Come on, come on, come on, come on!
Pick up the phone!

202
00:31:39.450 --> 00:31:44.345
<i>At the tone, please record your message.
When you finish recording, you may hang...</i>

203
00:31:56.133 --> 00:31:57.367
Rosie?

204
00:33:21.951 --> 00:33:23.753
Troy!

205
00:33:33.529 --> 00:33:37.087
You didn't happen to see Rosie
come by here in last hour or so, did you?

206
00:33:37.187 --> 00:33:39.737
Yeah, as a matter of fact, I did.
Caused quite a dust storm.

207
00:33:39.837 --> 00:33:42.980
Seemed she was in a big
old hurry to get somewhere.

208
00:33:45.841 --> 00:33:48.445
Yeah, see that?
That's why I don't mess with 'em.

209
00:33:48.545 --> 00:33:50.714
What's that?

210
00:33:50.814 --> 00:33:54.751
Pretty girls.
Will break your heart every time.

211
00:37:13.282 --> 00:37:15.085
Troy?

212
00:37:17.988 --> 00:37:20.222
Got those beers.

213
00:39:13.068 --> 00:39:15.471
You motherfucker.

214
00:44:24.346 --> 00:44:27.529
Fuck. Hey.

215
00:44:32.622 --> 00:44:35.024
Kid, you better get up.

216
00:44:53.309 --> 00:44:56.144
- You're not one of them?
- I'm not one of them.

217
00:44:56.244 --> 00:44:58.180
- You have to help me get out.
- I'm gonna help you.

218
00:44:58.280 --> 00:45:00.887
- Your last name, what's your name?
- I'm Sarah.

219
00:45:00.987 --> 00:45:04.344
- Sarah? They're not gonna hurt you.
- Please. They took my friend Cole.

220
00:45:04.444 --> 00:45:07.823
- You have to help me find him.
- I know, I know. I just saw him next door.

221
00:45:07.923 --> 00:45:12.265
No, that's not him. You have to find him.
You have to help him. Please.

222
00:45:12.365 --> 00:45:14.541
I'm going to.
I just need you to stay quiet, all right?

223
00:45:14.641 --> 00:45:18.062
- People don't make it out of here.
- Girl, you gotta be quiet, all right?

224
00:45:18.162 --> 00:45:21.169
- Okay.
- I'll be back.

225
00:45:31.947 --> 00:45:33.404
Shit!

226
00:45:34.584 --> 00:45:37.287
John! Holy shit. John, he's fucking crazy.

227
00:45:37.387 --> 00:45:41.291
- John... Help me, John, help me.
- Slow down. Slow down, slow down.

228
00:45:41.391 --> 00:45:44.352
John... get me out of here.

229
00:45:44.452 --> 00:45:47.129
Get me out of here, please!

230
00:45:47.229 --> 00:45:49.097
Please.

231
00:45:54.002 --> 00:45:57.874
- This lock, babe, I need bolt cutters.
- No, no, you don't. No, just break it off!

232
00:45:57.974 --> 00:46:01.520
Just break it the fuck off!
Get me out of here, John, please!

233
00:46:01.620 --> 00:46:03.586
Stop!

234
00:46:09.885 --> 00:46:11.349
Fuck.

235
00:46:15.958 --> 00:46:18.595
- Fuck.
- It's him. It's him. He's back.

236
00:46:18.695 --> 00:46:20.248
Fuck. He's back.

237
00:46:31.708 --> 00:46:35.378
- Fuck. John...
- I can take him.

238
00:46:35.878 --> 00:46:38.381
I'll stop this.

239
00:46:38.481 --> 00:46:40.534
- I can take him.
- Okay.

240
00:46:40.634 --> 00:46:44.399
He doesn't know that I'm here.
He's by himself.

241
00:46:44.499 --> 00:46:47.265
- John. Johnny.
- One blow and he's done.

242
00:46:49.726 --> 00:46:53.062
- I'll be back before you know it.
- Okay. John...

243
00:48:44.807 --> 00:48:47.075
About damn time.

244
00:48:52.014 --> 00:48:55.685
Well, which one of you dumbshits
forgot how to tie a slipknot?

245
00:48:55.785 --> 00:48:59.167
It's nice to see you, too, Daddy.
You got any aspirin?

246
00:48:59.267 --> 00:49:02.758
Aspirin? I'm the one who needs aspirin.

247
00:49:03.358 --> 00:49:06.081
I had that kid's dad on the hook for 50K.

248
00:49:06.181 --> 00:49:09.698
- Now we ain't got shit.
- You know, you didn't have to kill him.

249
00:49:09.798 --> 00:49:13.135
He saw my face.
What'd you expect me to do?

250
00:49:13.235 --> 00:49:15.772
I'm sorry, okay?

251
00:49:16.172 --> 00:49:20.910
- What do you want from me?
- You're gonna dig the damn hole. Alone.

